  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1207 AM CDT Sun Jun 28 2026\n\nHot and mainly dry conditions are forecast to continue through the \nextended forecast. For the first part of the next week an upper \nlevel ridge will be centered across eastern CONUS with an upper \nlevel trough across the western CONUS. This will result in highs in \nthe mid 90s to near 100 and overnight lows generally in the 70s. \nShowers and thunderstorms are forecast to develop along the western \nperiphery of the upper level ridge Monday afternoon and evening, \nmainly from the Trans-Pecos region into the Panhandle. This activity \nis forecast to generally remain west of the area, although a storm \nor two could sneak into western portions of Crockett County. \n\nThe aforementioned upper level ridge will then slowly shift east \nlate in the week as an upper level ridge strengthens across northern \nMexico and the Southwest United States. This will result in even \nhotter temperatures as we head into the holiday weekend. Highs \nThursday into Saturday will be in the upper 90s to near 105, while \novernight lows remain in the mid 70s to near 80.",
